bers, you can use .pow() to take the power of a tensor.",\n        "This avoids having to create a new tensor with .view() or .reshape().",\n        "Here\'s an example of how to use .pow():",\n        "# bad",\n        "torch.pow(A, 2)",\n        "# good"\n    ]\n}\nOutput: ', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct', 'n': 1, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.01}}
